+## v7 follow-up — directional Ultimate visual
+
+The v6 target-position `ViewEffect` nested under the DirDot fan is no longer used: the user’s screenshot showed repeated large slashes, one for each selected enemy. V7 instead registers one visual-only `LineRangeProjectile` using the cast direction and an `Animated` `view_projectiles` binding. The line applies no effects; the original DirDot hit selection and native lethal-counter remain intact. The line is 110,000 units long and 60,000 units wide; it reuses the original 201×122 Balmond slash art from v5, with the narrow point intended at Balmond and the broader flame toward the far end. These client visuals still require an in-game test.
+
+The visible S2 spin pixels are shrunk by 10% within each frame; the frame canvas, animation crop metadata, and combat logic are unchanged. See `docs/BALMOND_V7_VISUAL_AND_MOVEMENT_RESEARCH.md` for the Sion-Q and Garen movement findings.
